# Make an elf rogue and photograph the character sheet.
#
# One assertion: an elf's Search must carry the Sharp Senses inherent bonus,
# the same one its Spot and Listen already carry. lib/races.irh:1067-1068
# promises "+2 insight bonus to all sensory-based skills (Search, Spot, and
# Listen)" and grants only ABILITY(CA_SHARP_SENSES,2), lib/races.irh:952.
#
# A rogue, because a rogue has Search as a class skill and enough ranks that
# the line appears on the sheet at all.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes

# The choices are named, not counted, so a race or class added to lib/ cannot
# make this script build a different character. See @choose in src/Wposix.cpp.
@choose "Elf"
@choose "Elf (Standard)"
@choose "Rogue"
a                       # Attributes: the first of the five offered sets. The
                        #   sets have no names, so this one stays positional.
@choose "Neutral"       # and not [b] Neutral Good or [h] Neutral Evil
a                       # First feat.  Which feats are offered depends on the
a                       # Second feat. attribute rolls, so these stay counted.

RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y

y       # Do you wish to worship <god>? -- yes
a       # Personality archetype

ESC     # dismiss the arrival-room description; now in play
d       # character sheet
@expect "Race   Elf"    # the whole point of the run; stop here if it is wrong
W                       # Write Dump
s h e e t ENTER         # filename: "sheet"
@dump:afterdump
ESC
@quit
